              <p>The cost ranges most guides publish are national averages. National averages are not useful in Delaware County, where labor costs reflect the Philadelphia metro market premium and older housing stock adds scope complexity that flat per-square-foot numbers don't capture.</p>
              <p>The figures below are sourced from two places: the <strong>Remodeling Magazine Cost vs. Value Report (Philadelphia metro edition, 2026)</strong> for market benchmarks, and ProBrothers' own completed project history for the local reality check.</p>

